 ### Production follow-up
 Published Chromium computed none while preview computed URL. The installed Lightning CSS reproduced this when the standard declaration preceded an identical WebKit one: output retained only the unsupported prefixed property. Reversing equivalent declarations keeps both. Application CSS pairs now use prefixed-first/standard-last and verify-built-glass.mjs asserts standard SVG/substrate/fallback rules in the built artifact. Preview success alone was insufficient evidence for published optics.
+
+## L48 — hierarchy before more optics
+A transparent sticky source group allowed period text to pass under labels. It now stays in document flow, avoiding the collision without stacking fixes. Legacy sheet selectors were removed and replaced with one header/body/footer layout; desktop single-lap distance/time share a row, while mobile preserves the focus-friendly two-part input. Generic mobile 16px-important sizing explicitly excludes the time control so its 27px type survives.
+
+The optical registry now only tags intended filtered surfaces. Triggers and vertical navigation receive matching actual-filter rules, and built-artifact checks cover segment/triggers/menus/settings. A renderer flag is still insufficient proof; production computed checks are separate. Chromium tested all five sections in both themes, three iframe widths, source dragging, entry validation/focus, theme change with an open menu, and Escape containment. No native hardware/GPU equivalence is inferred.
